+//   Mario Kart World, 7,619 MB of RAM): one file of 39,936 MB, 40.7 GB written in about 6.5 minutes ([写盘], at least 74% of it bytes written again), in step with about 30 s
+//   of long frames outside NVN calls. nxnative measured the stall at the system's periodic flush growing with the file (a 16 GB M5 Mac with 1 GB touched: up to 148 ms with one
+//   20 GB file, 4 ms with twenty 1 GB files; on an iPhone, 7 min 33 s played with one file, 14 minutes without the 30-s stalls with 1 GB files).
+//   Same addresses and total size: window file k backs [g_base + k * chunk, + its size) from its offset 0, so an address's file and offset are arithmetic (gf_at); a range across
+//   two files is punched and mapped one file at a time, at contiguous addresses. s2a_guest_fd() stays the first file's descriptor: its callers only ask whether the window is
+//   in files (graphics/nvn nvn_mtl.m mem_any_touched, the [写盘] line, the unit tests); s2a_guest_file_at gives the file and offset of an address.
+//   Ported (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds) from seedds/nxnative 0c078130 (dm/host/hle_svc.c:69-81 the chunk switch and the file table, :91-99 the offset to file arithmetic
+//   of guest_file_punch, :189 the st_blocks sum, :234-265 guest_files_map, :278-285 the chunk size rule); first in its commits 865cc35f and 8d5d4f1b
+#define GF_MAX 1024                 // nxnative's GF_MAX: the chunk is raised so that the window takes at most this many files
+#define GF_MIN_CHUNK (64ull << 20)  // nxnative's minimum chunk (DM_GUEST_FILE_CHUNK at least 64M)
+static int g_gf_fd[GF_MAX];         // the window's files, open for reading and writing (g_gf_fd[0] == g_gfd)
+static _Atomic int g_gf_n;          // how many (0 = the guest is not in files); stored with release once g_gf_fd, g_gf_chunk and g_gf_span are set
+static uint64_t g_gf_chunk;         // each window file's size, the last one's being the rest of g_gf_span (one file: g_gf_chunk == g_gf_span)
+static uint64_t g_gf_span;          // the window size mapped from the files (g_size then; s2a_window_trim may shrink g_size later, never the files)
